    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0563" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/12571: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-21T18:00:00+09:00"
                            >December 21, 1918—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 21—12:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram December 19, 4 p.m. Since the publication of the interview reported
                    in my telegram of November 3, 1 p.m.,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d378-f1"/> Okuma has
                    made no public statement with reference to Japan’s ambitions in the South Sea
                    Islands. Reports in the American press are probably based on a special interview
                    granted their representative which were [<hi rendition="#italic">was</hi>] not
                    given out in Japan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
